	(lib_symbols)
	(text "POWER AND DRIVERS  (owner: Eeshan for now, open to a new member). The whole sheet is 'Exclude from board': none of it is on the HAT PCB.\nDon't rename or delete the labels. They are the cables from the HAT's two driver terminals.\n\nWHAT GOES ON THIS SHEET\n  Battery (12.8V LiFePO4) → 20A inline fuse → kill switch → WUPP fuse block\n      → 10A branch: Pegasus Pocket Powerbox Advance Gen 2\n      → 10A branch: Mean Well SD-50A-24 (24V) → both DM542T drivers, 1000 µF across each driver's supply → motors\n  Each DM542T: PUL- / DIR- / ENA- from the labels on the left. PUL+ / DIR+ / ENA+ to +5V. Logic selector set to 5V.\n  GND on this sheet = the Pi's ground. Name any other ground (e.g. BATT-, 24V_RTN) unless it really is wired to the Pi's ground.\n  The DM542T, PPBA and fuse block have no KiCad symbol: use a Connector_Generic block with the terminal names, or make one."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
